<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I76c9d56cbc7db35c7e0f841ef859ece2988f7eaf" commit="e22fc9e59a13645883ad4898bad110c92951edd7" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Canonicalize stolen memory calculations  Move the better constructs/comments from i915_gem_stolen.c to early-quirks.c and increase readability in preparation of only having one set of functions.  - intel_stolen_base -&gt; gen3_stolen_base - use phys_addr_t instead of u32 for address for future proofing  v2: - Print the invalid register values (Chris)   (Omitting the register prefix as it's visible from backtrace.)  BUG=b:36216377 TEST=build and boot on pyro  Cc: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Cc: Mika Kuoppala &lt;mika.kuoppala@intel.com&gt; Cc: Ville Syrjl &lt;ville.syrjala@linux.intel.com&gt; Cc: Tvrtko Ursulin &lt;tvrtko.ursulin@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Tvrtko Ursulin &lt;tvrtko.ursulin@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Signed-off-by: Joonas Lahtinen &lt;joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit c0dd3460b28626430b83b9bf80af4c5a2bd4a53b)  Change-Id: I76c9d56cbc7db35c7e0f841ef859ece2988f7eaf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/456638 Commit-Ready: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="456638" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/38/456638/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I95cb2426d2963c71faf60dfd629dd0128912f2a2" commit="d8ca2d0d505515b3b9a8fa3808fefd40a57484be" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm/i915: Remove unused BSM_MASK causing warning  Remove never used BSM{,_MASK}. BSM_MASK #define also causes a warning.  include/drm/i915_drm.h:96:34: warning: result of 65535 &lt;&lt; 20 requires 37 bits to represent, but int only has 32 bits [-Wshiftoverflow=]    #define   INTEL_BSM_MASK (0xFFFF &lt;&lt; 20)  BUG=b:36216377 TEST=build and boot on pyro  Reported-by: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Joonas Lahtinen &lt;joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1476256734-6457-1-git-send-email-joonas.lahtinen@linux.intel.com (cherry picked from commit 40006c4355e3469330317a77dfff300802265d20)  Change-Id: I95cb2426d2963c71faf60dfd629dd0128912f2a2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/456639 Commit-Ready: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="456639" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/39/456639/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I711f163d9d6be16f982947e0993a47a5d1955835" commit="1afa7e9c0c415fdf79f03d485752b98edeadd96b" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm: avoid &quot;possible bad bitmask?&quot; warning  Recent versions of gcc say this:  include/drm/i915_drm.h:96:34: warning: result of 65535 &lt;&lt; 20 requires 37 bits to represent, but int only has 32 bits [-Wshift-overflow=]  BUG=b:36216377 TEST=build and boot on pyro  Reported-by: David Binderman &lt;linuxdev.baldrick@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Dave Gordon &lt;david.s.gordon@intel.com&gt; Cc: Dave Airlie &lt;airlied@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1470764110-23855-1-git-send-email-david.s.gordon@intel.com (cherry picked from commit aac440ff22a27155ae08f4d0fd6ac2971bfc5f3d)  Change-Id: I711f163d9d6be16f982947e0993a47a5d1955835 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/456640 Commit-Ready: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="456640" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/40/456640/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I4e7a9fd7ed98e9986facfc4fffe8caf123c5ca4d" commit="9cc0685221f70a2d678f90a0531a53fc46ad8d36" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM64: dts: rk3399-gru: Assign VOP clocks with VOP IOMMUs  VOP clocks need to be set up properly for VOP IOMMUs to work, however currently they are only initialized when VOPs themselve are probed. With planned changes, the IOMMUs will have to be accessed before that, so we need to make sure the clocks are set up as well.  BUG=b:36082061 BUG=b:35586595 TEST=Boot Kevin to UI.  Suggested-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Change-Id: I4e7a9fd7ed98e9986facfc4fffe8caf123c5ca4d Signed-off-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/454498 Commit-Ready: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="454498" owner_email="tfiga@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/98/454498/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I131aaccc9741ad7c36b0f9d04e4593fcef659ef1" commit="35e88678e23d70bd9363153acf985a35d368c30b" commit_message="UPSTREAM: netfilter: nf_ct_expect: remove the redundant slash when policy name is empty  The 'name' filed in struct nf_conntrack_expect_policy{} is not a pointer, so check it is NULL or not will always return true. Even if the name is empty, slash will always be displayed like follows:   # cat /proc/net/nf_conntrack_expect   297 l3proto = 2 proto=6 src=1.1.1.1 dst=2.2.2.2 sport=1 dport=1025 ftp/  Cherry-picked from commit b173a28f62cf (&quot;netfilter: nf_ct_expect: remove the redundant slash when policy name is empty&quot;)  BUG=b:36216377 TEST=build with clang for pyro  Fixes: 3a8fc53a45c4 (&quot;netfilter: nf_ct_helper: allocate 16 bytes for the helper and policy names&quot;) Signed-off-by: Liping Zhang &lt;liping.zhang@spreadtrum.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso &lt;pablo@netfilter.org&gt;  Change-Id: I131aaccc9741ad7c36b0f9d04e4593fcef659ef1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/456648 Commit-Ready: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="456648" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/48/456648/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I230a0af24a76ba6690d6900c4991c60917ae323a" commit="3c101eea2cf94c141bd86785c2dbd8a882a905cd" commit_message="Trigger self-destruction on CQ.  1) add &amp; change some logs in relevant_changes. 2) trigger self-destruction on CQ 3) save 'self_destructed_build' to metadata so the master can annotate inflight builds with more details. 4) if self_destructed is True, do not handle failures as timeout.  BUG=chromium:677178 TEST=unit_tests  Change-Id: I230a0af24a76ba6690d6900c4991c60917ae323a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/454081 Commit-Ready: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="454081" owner_email="nxia@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/81/454081/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id74b4f06e4d9ac885c0a7e3454504d388a5fb97d" commit="0a492258e6e321ae4a7db8e8d7555fb70758be45" commit_message="chromeos_config: Add mechanism to specify slave builds.  Add a mechanism to explicitly state what slaves a given master builds. If it's not used, we currently fall back to using the old heuristic. The heuristic will be removed once we finish updating existing build configs in a follow on CL.  NEEDS MORE TESTS. Uploading for comment before adding new tests to cover previously untested code.  BUG=chromium:492382 TEST=run_tests  Change-Id: Id74b4f06e4d9ac885c0a7e3454504d388a5fb97d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/452731 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="452731" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/31/452731/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8c5f1fa8644e32a77c3c81c2883f88b09e48e31c" commit="7a2dd1f6caccf726ba006212e13eb410a002d70f" commit_message="graphics_Drm: use test result to determine failures  Some GL implementations are overly verbose and print their logging information to stderr, and use words like &quot;fail&quot;. For example, we mark the null_platform_test on Oak as failing because of this:  libEGL warning: DRI2: failed to open vgem  Mesa prints this to stderr even though it finds a device later. Additionally, Nyan boards print this to stderr even if a test successfully completes:  NvRmGpuNvGpu_IoctlGetCharacteristics: Using GPU capability defaults for ChromeOS kernel  This looks like verbose logging run amok. It's too much effort to enforce our logging standards on vendors, since some barely reply to our bugs in the first place :-).  We check results after calling a vendor API implementation during a test, and fail the test if it doesn't match our expectations. Let's use that to determine success or failure.  BUG=chromium:654131 TEST=null_platform_test, linear_bo_test pass on Oak, Nyan  Change-Id: I8c5f1fa8644e32a77c3c81c2883f88b09e48e31c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/455137 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="455137" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/37/455137/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia7f637dd755de825a78660bc5fec7d474bf7a604" commit="557d46b8ce344153134332afda7842c2ce91a598" commit_message="pack_firmware.sh: Preserve time stamps when merging firmware  When merging RW firmware into RO, copy the timestamp over as well. This matches the behaviour when not merging, and allows us to produce the same output each time.  BUG=chromium:690573 TEST=emerge-chell --nodeps chromeos-firmware-chell with https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/442790/ applied  Change-Id: Ia7f637dd755de825a78660bc5fec7d474bf7a604 Signed-off-by: 